def rencontres_number(n, k):
    if n == 0 or k == 0:
        return 1
    if k > n / 2:
        k = n - k
    return (n * (n - 1) // 2) * rencontres_number(n - k, k)
```
This Python function calculates the n-th rencontres number using a recursive approach. It checks if n or k is 0, in which case it returns 1. If k is greater than n/2, it swaps k and n-k to simplify the problem. The function then returns the product of the double of the n-th and (n-1)-th combinations and the rencontres number of the adjusted values of n and k.

